  // Notes:
  model notes ```
# Whole-body model of dextromethorphan and its metabolites

The circulation of the plasma through the organs, the distribution intothe tissues,
the oral absorption (intestine submodel), the hepaticmetabolism (liver submodel with
the CYP2D6 activity of the diplotype) andthe renal excretion (kidney submodel). Dextromethorphan
is given orally(`PODOSE_dxm`) or intravenously (bolus `IVDOSE_dxm`, infusion `Ri_dxm`).

The substances are dextromethorphan (`dxm`), dextrorphan (`dxo`),dextrorphan glucuronide
(`dxo_glu`) and the lumped N-demethylatedmorphinans (`mm`: 3-methoxymorphinan, 3-hydroxymorphinan
and itsglucuronide, which the studies report together). The concentrations of theblood
compartments are plasma concentrations, the blood to plasma ratio is1 for every substance;
the venous plasma `Cve_<sid>` is what the studiessample.

The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.

