```
  BW_ref notes ```
Body weight at which the exchange flows of the tissue distribution (`ftissue_<sid>`) are given;
they scale with the body weight as the volumes, the blood flows and the renal clearance
do.
```
  FQgu notes ```
FQgu is the sum of FQgu + FQsp + FQpa for the correct portal bloodflow, with FQgu=0.146,
FQsp=0.017, FQpa=0.017.
```
  ftissue_fast notes ```
The exchange flow between the plasma and the tissue of the liver,the kidney and the
gut at the reference body weight `BW_ref`:fast against their perfusion, so the exchange
does not limit thehepatic metabolism, the renal excretion or the absorption. Fixed.
```
  f_GFR_Qki notes ```
GFR per renal blood flow (76.3 ml/l). Calibrated so that thehealthy GFR is 101 ml/min
at the renal blood flow of 1.32354 l/minof 75 kg, the normal GFR of the classes of
renal impairment(`pkpdsim.impairment`).
```
  GFR_base notes ```
The GFR of healthy kidneys, which scales with the renal blood flowand so with the
body weight; the GFR is `KI__f_renal_function`times this rate.
```
  ftissue_dxm notes ```
Exchange flow between the plasma and the tissue of the peripheral organs (the rest
of the body, the lung) at the reference body weight `BW_ref`; it sets how fast the distribution
phase is.
```
  ftissue_dxo notes ```
Exchange flow between the plasma and the tissue of the peripheral organs (the rest
of the body, the lung) at the reference body weight `BW_ref`; it sets how fast the distribution
phase is.
```
  ftissue_dxo_glu notes ```
Exchange flow between the plasma and the tissue of the peripheral organs (the rest
of the body, the lung) at the reference body weight `BW_ref`; it sets how fast the distribution
phase is.
```
  ftissue_mm notes ```
Exchange flow between the plasma and the tissue of the peripheral organs (the rest
of the body, the lung) at the reference body weight `BW_ref`; it sets how fast the distribution
phase is.
```
  KI__f_renal_function notes ```
>
> 1.0: increased kidney function
> 1.0: normal kidney function (healthy control)
> <1.0: decreased kidney function
>
> 
Renal function relative to the healthy glomerular filtration rate`GFR_base`, which is 101
ml/min at 75 kg; a measured creatinineclearance of X ml/min is the renal function
X/101.
```
  LI__f_cyp2d6 notes ```
Activity of CYP2D6 relative to the reference (1.0, no interactingdrug), set by the
experiments for an interaction, never fitted. Theactivity of CYP2D6 of a diplotype
is the activity score`cyp2d6_activity` of the CYP2D6 submodel, which this factor multiplies.
```
  LI__f_cyp3a4 notes ```
Activity of CYP3A4 relative to the reference (1.0, no interactingdrug), set by the
experiments for an interaction, never fitted. Theactivity of CYP2D6 of a diplotype
is the activity score`cyp2d6_activity` of the CYP2D6 submodel, which this factor multiplies.
```
  LI__f_ugt2b15 notes ```
Activity of UGT2B15 relative to the reference (1.0, no interactingdrug), set by the
experiments for an interaction, never fitted. Theactivity of CYP2D6 of a diplotype
is the activity score`cyp2d6_activity` of the CYP2D6 submodel, which this factor multiplies.
```
  LI__cyp2d6_activity_ref notes ```
The activity score of a diplotype of two fully functional alleles(\*1/\*1), at which
the maximal rate `DXMCYP2D6_Vmax` is given: the rateof the O-demethylation by CYP2D6 scales linearly
with`cyp2d6_activity/cyp2d6_activity_ref`.
```
  LI__DXMCYP2D6_Vmax notes "Maximal rate per liver volume."
  LI__DXMCYP2D6_Km_dxm notes ```
Of the order of the values of human liver microsomes, fixed: the hepatic concentrations
are far below it, the kinetics are linear.
```
  LI__DXMCYPX_Vmax notes "Maximal rate per liver volume."
  LI__DXMCYPX_Km_dxm notes ```
Of the order of the values of human liver microsomes, fixed: the hepatic concentrations
are far below it, the kinetics are linear.
```
  LI__DXMNDM_Vmax notes "Maximal rate per liver volume."
  LI__DXMNDM_Km_dxm notes ```
Of the order of the values of human liver microsomes, fixed: the hepatic concentrations
are far below it, the kinetics are linear.
```
  LI__DXONDM_Vmax notes "Maximal rate per liver volume."
  LI__DXONDM_Km_dxo notes ```
Of the order of the values of human liver microsomes, fixed: the hepatic concentrations
are far below it, the kinetics are linear.
```
  LI__DXOUGT_Vmax notes "Maximal rate per liver volume."
  LI__DXOUGT_Km_dxo notes ```
Of the order of the values of human liver microsomes, fixed: the hepatic concentrations
are far below it, the kinetics are linear.
```
  GU__F_dxm_abs notes ```
The fraction of the dextromethorphan in the lumen which is absorbed,`(1 - F_dxm_abs)` is excreted
in the feces; fitted on theurinary recoveries.
```
  GU__DXMABS_k notes ```
Fixed: the step is in series with the dissolution and is not identified apart from
it.
```
  LI__DXMCYP2D6 notes ```
O-demethylation of dextromethorphan to dextrorphan (CYP2D6), the pathway of the metabolizer
phenotype: it is most of the clearance of extensive metabolizers and absent in poor
metabolizers.
```
  LI__DXMCYPX notes ```
CYP2D6-independent O-demethylation of dextromethorphan to dextrorphan (CYP3A4, CYP2C9),
the low affinity site of the microsomes; it forms the dextrorphan of poor metabolizers.
```
  LI__DXMNDM notes ```
N-demethylation of dextromethorphan to 3-methoxymorphinan (CYP3A4), the main CYP2D6-independent
clearance of dextromethorphan.
```
  LI__DXONDM notes ```
N-demethylation of dextrorphan to 3-hydroxymorphinan (CYP3A4); 3-hydroxymorphinan
is about 16 % of an oral dose in the urine of extensive metabolizers (Capon1996,
Schadel1995).
```
  LI__DXOUGT notes ```
Glucuronidation of dextrorphan (UGT2B15), the main route of the dextrorphan which
is formed: about 96 % of the dextrorphan of the plasma is conjugated (Nagai1996).
